{title: 292 - Jesus, I Come}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]Out of my bondage, [C]sorrow and [G]night,
[G]Jesus, I [D7]come, Jesus, I [G]come;
[G]Into Thy freedom, [C]gladness and [G]light,
[G]Jesus, I come [D7]to [G]Thee;
[C]Out of my sickness [G]into Thy health,
[C]Out of my want and [A7]into Thy [D]wealth[D7],
[G]Out of my sin and [C]into Thy[G]self,
[G]Jesus, I come [D7]to [G]Thee.

Verse 2:
[G]Out of [C]my shameful [G]failure and loss,
[G]Jesus, I [D7]come, Jesus, [G]I come;
[G]Into the [C]glorious gain [G]of Thy cross,
[G]Jesus, [D7]I come [G]to Thee;
[C]Out of earth's [G]sorrows into Thy balm,
[C]Out of [A7]life's storms [D]and into [D7]Thy calm,
[G]Out of [C]distress to [G]jubilant psalm,
[G]Jesus, [D7]I come [G]to Thee.

Verse 3:
[G]Out of [C]unrest and [G]arrogant pride,
[G]Jesus, I [D7]come, Jesus, [G]I come;
[G]Into Thy [C]blessed will [G]to abide,
[G]Jesus, [D7]I come [G]to Thee;
[C]Out of myself to [G]dwell in Thy love,
[C]Out [A7]of despair [D]into [D7]raptures above,
[G]Upward for [C]aye on wings [G]like a dove,
[G]Jesus, [D7]I come [G]to Thee.

Verse 4:
[G]Out of the [C]fear and dread [G]of the tomb,
[G]Jesus, I [D7]come, Jesus, [G]I come;
[G]Into the [C]joy and light [G]of Thy home,
[G]Jesus, [D7]I come [G]to Thee;
[C]Out of the [G]depths of ruin untold,
[C]Into [A7]the peace [D]of Thy [D7]sheltering fold,
[G]Ever Thy [C]glorious face [G]to behold,
[G]Jesus, [D7]I come [G]to Thee.
